      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T09:22:18Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(motion): Adaptive clears the rotary developed wrap level by level, under the load and kink laws\n\nThe rotary wrap ladder no longer rewrites Adaptive to Offset rings: each\ndeveloped level runs the HSM planner, and every developed arc is chorded\nbefore wrapping, so each world move is posed radially. A seam law\n(hsm::Seam, period 2*pi*R_ref per cover) refuses Adaptive by name for a\nlevel whose centre component reaches a cover end short of a full lap;\nany planner refusal on the wrap names \"the developed level at radius R\"\nand Offset rings cut that level. Offset rings themselves are unchanged\n(digest pinned against main).\n\nReadings (release; r6 wall / r5 neck bar in r7 stock, BN D6, leave 0.5,\nstepdown 0.5, Helix r1; law 14.6 % D + 35 % = 19.7 %): radius 6.5 and\n6.0 - 22,528 moves, 19.5 % D, 0 breaks past 5 deg; 5.5 - 7,416 moves,\n18.8 % D, 0 breaks; 5.0 refused by the planning budget, rings cut it.\nNo planner overload note (Plunge entry read 76.8 % D in round 1).\n\nTests (rotary_adaptive): adaptive_plans_the_developed_levels_under_the_load_and_kink_laws\nand the_developed_window_reaches_the_planner_and_names_each_refusal\n(heavy lane), offset_rings_on_the_wrap_are_the_program_they_always_were\n(debug); machining3d::hsm::tests::the_seam_cuts_an_area_at_a_cover_end_short_of_a_lap.\nFollow-ups: #54 (D-flat wrap, seam end-to-end), #55 (r6.2 levels, helix\noverload, load margin).\n\nFixes #9\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
