      "message": "fix(motion): the rotary Adaptive wrap holds the kink law on its posted chords, and names every ring-cut level\n\nReview fixes on PR #57:\n- wrap_exit chords each developed XY arc under Adaptive at a 4 deg\n  angular cap as well as the sagitta, with 0.01 mm end chords so arc\n  junctions gain next to nothing. OffsetRings keeps sagitta-only chords.\n- The heavy test pulls the world program back into the developed frame\n  and reads its in-cut breaks. Whole bar: sagitta only, 98,525 world\n  moves and 12,824 breaks past 5 deg on the planned levels; 4 deg cap,\n  160,989 moves and 0 breaks. (A 2.5 deg cap with full-step end chords\n  left 14 junction breaks at 138,097 moves.)\n- A ring-cut level is read from the program's shape (a cut level with\n  no proved arc) and must carry its named note. A named level must post\n  no arc. The old check read ring-cut from that same note.\n- A hard planner error on the wrap falls back to rings for that level,\n  with a named note. The planar ladder still propagates it.\n- The proof-tally note says \"the developed level at radius R\" on the wrap.\n- The rings digest hashes on a 1e-6 lattice and is re-pinned. The old\n  bitwise digest still matched on the same build.\n- The test file has a provenance header.\n\nRefs #9\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
